"text":"The edge depth-first search of an undirected graph: a sequence of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EdgeDepthFirstSearchEvent"},{"text":"s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that reports each edge once, by its position, from the end that reaches it first. The tree","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"edge into a vertex is not reported again from it, so a parallel edge to the parent is a back","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"edge. It holds a copy of the graph and can be iterated more than once, and keeps its own stack.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","title":"UndirectedEdgeDepthFirstSearch","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Traversal/documentation/Traversal":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal","type":"topic","title":"Traversal","abstract":[],"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/traversal","kind":"symbol"}}}